{19}{483l The spectre of Prohibition has risen once again, as Parliament considers a Bill to ban the sales of Spirits in the confines of the City proper. Supporters of the Bill cite increased Crime and Work Absenteeism figures as the principle Show of Cause for the bill, while its Critics cite similar Statistics during the last Prohibition era over 30 years ago.}
{1083}{483l 	Any citizen with information pertaining to the case should contact the Chief Inspector at 5 Saints Ave. immediately.}	
{1213}{483l	Mr. Terwilliger gained notoriety with the publication of his controversial novel "Horror Among the Dark Elves", when he made every effort to assure the public that the work was indeed based on factual evidence.  However, much to Mr. Terwilliger's dismay, discerning minds deemed the book to be a work of fiction in its entirety.  Mr. Terwilliger's publicist announced that the troubled author had recently been undergoing treatments to aid with the ongoing delusions that someone was attempting to murder him for publishing his work.
{1316}{483l 	The spectre of Prohibition has risen once again, as the Governor considers a Bill to ban the sales of Spirits in the confines of the City proper. Supporters of the Bill cite increased Crime and Work Absenteeism figures as the principle Show of Cause for the bill, while its Critics cite similar Statistics during the last Prohibition era over 30 years ago.}
{76000}{486c The Siegfried-Maginot expedition is setting off!}
{76001}{492c _ THE VALLEY OF THE EXILES: MYTH OR REALITY? _}
{76002}{483l After months of preparation, Professors Siegfried and Maginot, distinguished graduates of the University of Archaeology in Tarante, are about to embark on an expedition to locate the (legendary) Valley of the Exiles. It takes its name from the Boutchiks, a small group of people said to have lived there centuries ago who were banished from the rest of the world and exiled, along with their king, Malabar V, to this prison-like valley. Long forgotten by all, the valley appears to have been rediscovered by the two scientists following extensive library research. Their goal is to uncover the remains of this civilization and understand the reasons that drove the Boutchiks to resign themselves to such an exile. As the expedition has sparked heated debate regarding the scientific credibility of the venture, Siegfried and Maginot have deemed it unnecessary to reveal their itinerary, let alone their destination...}
